=== ui_errors / logcat check ===
At 320dp/1.3x on item_that_you_love_view.dart and store_screen.dart: ZERO
"RenderFlex overflowed on the bottom" lines from item_widget.dart's detail Column.
(One unrelated overflow WAS observed from a 3rd-party package,
animated_flip_counter-0.3.4/lib/animated_flip_counter.dart:210, "overflowed by
21/36 pixels on the RIGHT" — different widget, different axis, pre-existing,
unrelated to this fix; logged separately as a regression-candidate.)

CONCLUSION: the literal AC1 sub-clause ("zero RenderFlex overflowed on the
bottom logcat line") is satisfied, but the second sub-clause ("matched against
the DLS/Stitch frame") is NOT: the product name is squeezed into an ~4-12dp
box (well under half a natural text line) and renders as illegible dash-like
fragments / letter-top-only clipping, on 2 of the 3 named consumers, LTR and
RTL, confirmed both by direct screenshot crop and by live render-tree
introspection. Root cause: the fix's fixed 13dp reclaim (8dp spacer + 2dp +
3dp paddings) is far smaller than the actual vertical growth of the Column's
non-flexible siblings at 1.3x scale (e.g. the unit-type text alone grows from
~12dp to ~25dp natural height), so the Flexible name Row is starved of space.
Flutter's Flex algorithm satisfies this silently (Flexible + fit:loose) rather
than throwing a RenderFlex overflow assertion, which is why the log stays
clean even though the visual result fails the design match.
